# App Store Connect credentials for `make testflight`.
#
# Copy to .env (gitignored) and fill in. Two forms are supported:
#
# 1. 1Password references — the Makefile detects `op://` and runs release.sh
#    under `op run`, which resolves them into the child process environment only.
#    Never written to disk, and masked in output.
# 2. Plain values — used as-is, no 1Password needed.
#
# The key ID and issuer ID come from
# https://appstoreconnect.apple.com/access/integrations/api
# (an Account-scoped key, Developer role or higher — an App-scoped key cannot
# create the provisioning profiles -allowProvisioningUpdates needs).

ASC_API_KEY_ID=op://Provenance/AppStoreConnect/key_id
ASC_API_ISSUER_ID=op://Provenance/AppStoreConnect/issuer_id

# Provide ONE of the following.
#
# The .p8 on disk. If you drop it at
# ~/.appstoreconnect/private_keys/AuthKey_<KEY_ID>.p8 you can omit this entirely
# — release.sh looks there automatically.
# ASC_API_KEY_PATH=/Users/you/.appstoreconnect/private_keys/AuthKey_XXXXXXXXXX.p8
#
# Or the key contents, raw PEM or base64. release.sh sniffs which.
ASC_API_KEY_CONTENT=op://Provenance/AppStoreConnect/private_key
